            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI can not reproduce. Calling `MiniStarter.refresh()` indeed is needed for items to be updated. Here is the demo with the default `require('mini.starter').setup()`:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/587a5426-f8c6-4579-9caf-891f40858a71\r\n\r\nThe behavior you describe *can* happen if items are computed during startup. However, all examples (even this [one](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f0d6e89515c6b055c20d257da717bd30211532f1/doc/mini-starter.txt#L96)) are wrapped inside a function which is recomputed after `MiniStarter.refresh()`.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nCould you, please, share how you set up 'mini.starter' and 'mini.sessions'?",
