        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> As shown on your screen, I also have no issues during testing. I set a specific keymap to trigger session deletion and refresh, but it is not working.\r\n\r\nI see. I still can not reproduce this, but probably for a known reason.\r\n\r\nThe `MiniSessions.select()` [uses `vim.ui.select()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f0d6e89515c6b055c20d257da717bd30211532f1/doc/mini-sessions.txt#L205-L207) function which is by design overridable and designed to allow asynchronous (i.e. code doesn't \"wait\" for function to finish but instead executes callback after selection is done) implementation. Probably you have it overridden by Telescope or some other asynchronous implementation, which means that `session.select('delete')` returns immediately and the next `starter.refresh()` is executed *before session is actually deleted*.\r\n\r\nUsing synchronous `vim.ui.select` implementation (i.e. code \"waits\" for the function to finish) like default or [`MiniPick.ui_select()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f0d6e89515c6b055c20d257da717bd30211532f1/doc/mini-pick.txt#L1037) should make \"Delete Sessions\" function refresh Starter buffer as expected.\r\n\r\nIf you want to keep using your current `vim.ui.select()` implementation, there are several options:\r\n- Accept that 'mini.starter' \"Sessions\" section will not update immediately.\r\n- Call `MiniStarter.refresh()` manually *after* deleting session.\r\n- Use manual implementation instead of `MiniSessions.select('delete')`. Something like this:\r\n    ```lua\r\n    -- Use this function as right hand side of the `<Leader>qd` mapping\r\n    local del = function()\r\n      local detected_names = vim.tbl_map(function(x) return x.name end, vim.tbl_values(MiniSessions.detected))\r\n      table.sort(detected_names)\r\n\r\n      local callback = function(item)\r\n        if item == nil then return end\r\n        MiniSessions.delete(item)\r\n        MiniStarter.refresh()\r\n      end\r\n      vim.ui.select(detected_names, { prompt = 'Select session to delete' }, callback)\r\n    end\r\n    ```",
